final fantasy xiv's latest expansion and  walkers almost here releasing on  november 23rd or the 19th if you're a  fan of early access it's set to finish  up a massive storyline spanning over 10  years and is the game's fourth expansion  after the reworked a realm reborn i got  invited to a preview event being held to  get some hands-on time with the new  reaper and sage jobs and of course it's  important to note that everything here  that i'm talking about is based off an  in development build final fantasy 14  and walker and any content is subject to  change before we actually get our hands  on the final version of the expansion  the event itself was set up to let us  run around and test jobs both new and  old while doing fates and hunts and two  new zones garlemald and thavnir old  charlene was also available as for us to  explore and meet up with people to run  the tower of zot the one dungeon that  was available in the preview build  while i didn't find any hunts i did run  the dungeon multiple times with a few  people on a few different jobs also  while trying out the new and improved  truss system also spent a good amount of  time with target dummies on a very  scenic beach in that near just trying  out jobs that i wanted to see the  changes that they made too i feel like  it's important to let you know that i'm  a tank mate at heart i spent most of my  time playing reaper and i do have  impressions for sage as well but healing  really isn't my strongest suit i didn't  even get to take the sage into a dungeon  run for example also i'm not going to be  getting super technical in my breakdown  at all all of these numbers and the math  on the skills as we were presented them  could change anyways so i'm going to  just focus mainly on how the jobs felt  to play i feel like that this is more  important than just the numbers  after getting my hands on both of the  new jobs my biggest takeaway was how  much they both feel fresh and different  in terms of both style and how they play  stage even more so given that it has to  fall under this new healer split of pure  healers and shield healers reaper even  does a lot to stand out against most of  the other physical melee jobs with its  multiple meters and keeping track of  weaving scythe attacks and avatar  attacks both jobs are very flashy and i  feel they are a great showcase of how  far the game has come both in terms of  design visually and mechanically they  both offer something that feels familiar  to fans of their specific roles but have  enough job specific identity to make the  overall experience of using them stand  out as a fun and enjoyable one overall i  feel they're excellent additions to the  existing jobs in the game and i cannot  wait to play them more once the  expansion is finally in my hands  i know i already talked a bit about how  much i'm not the biggest fan of healing  but my first reaction after messing  around with the skills for sage was that  i may have to change that everything  from the gundam inspired weapon design  to the wild and flashy animations even  the sound effects going off constantly  sound like they could be ripped right  out of the future  [Music]  they all come together to make this  really rad feeling here that plays  differently from all the other ones i  have experience with being able to mark  a party member with the cardia skill so  that they are passively receiving heals  while i'm getting carried away shooting  laser beams everywhere is exactly what  i'm looking for of course i want to make  sure my friends stay alive but i also  want to look good while i'm doing it and  that's exactly what it feels like the  sage is giving me they also have this  really cool gap closing ability called  icarus that can be used to propel  yourself towards enemies and allies  alike i'll probably end up using this  too much just because of how sick it  looks overall though i think my favorite  sage ability is and please forgive my  pronunciation of this eucrazia it  augments three of your abilities to be  more powerful versions of themselves in  other words it makes my existing lasers  into even bigger lasers and honestly who  doesn't want that my time with stage  left me wanting more and maybe even  considering spending more time in the  healing role itself even with the  anxiety that the responsibility gives me  final fantasy 14 did help me get over my  tank anxiety after all and it would make  sense that it would also probably do the  same for healing and if that isn't a  great endorsement of a new job i really  don't know what is reaper's a job i  spent most of my time with during the  preview event and the first time that i  got in shroud to proc and i became  enshrouded or as i like to endearingly  call it shifting into bad boy mode since  it visually changes your normally cheery  warrior of light into an angry red-eyed  shadow of the hedgehog void scent  version of yourself i knew i had a new  favorite melee dps job everything you  can do on reaper just feels so dang  badass the sick factor isn't even  limited to living out your dream of  being a scythe-wielding hot-topic-fueled  nightmare creature the feeling of  weaving your way through the reaper's  various abilities to get into that bad  boy mode just feels great  around all the core attacks you have  this really fun toolkit that also allows  you to do all sorts of fun stuff like  dash and teleport as well  [Music]  the thing that i really like the most  was just how awesome the reaper looks in  motion all of your attacks have these  really cool red or blue tearing effects  that follow your scythe movements and  they'll change depending on whatever  ability you're using this effect is only  amplified when you actually shift into  bad boy mode and go absolutely crazy  slashing everywhere where your warrior  of light is completely surrounded by  twice as many of these bright red and  black colored tears while you're  whipping your scythe around wildly and i  just love every second of it reaper is  kind of a natural step for me too since  my current favorite melee dps class is  dragoon and while they still kind of  function a little differently i think  there's enough to kind of bridge that  gap they also ended up sharing the same  armor too so i already have a really  nice back catalog of cool glamours to  use already and that's the most  important thing my love and loyalty to  tanking ultimately means that i don't  think i'll be switching over to being a  reaper main but you bet this is one of  the first alt jobs i'm going to level up  it could very easily be my second  favorite job i've played even with the  few hours i've had to learn it there's  still so much more of end walker for me  to see even with what little i had i  still wanted to try out so many other  jobs and do so many other things i  wanted to explore more of the great  desolate ruins of garland mold i wanted  to just sit and vibe on the beach in the  avenue for a while longer and take in  that amazing soundtrack some more  because man that new end walker motif is  so so good  [Music]  i can already feel it pulling on my  emotions even without the memories or  scenes attached to them but sadly  there's not enough time nevertheless i  still played enough to get me  exceedingly stoked for the adventure  that we're all going to be going on  together once end walker finally drops  buckle up fellow warriors of light we've  got a god to kill and a story to wrap up  and i hope to see you there for those  we've lost and for those we've yet to  save oh if you do see an extremely  handsome rogan named phil pwiskin and  the party finder say hi i promise i'll  do my best to tank the dungeon for you  also if you've made it this far and you  enjoyed what you've watched please leave  a like and a comment if you do they  might let me make more final fantasy  stuff between you and me that's exactly  what i want to do  [Music]  you
 

